  "steps": [
   "Heat the oven to 220°C (200°C fan) and dust a baking tray with flour.",
   "Mix the flour, baking powder, salt, paprika and a good grind of pepper in a large bowl. Rub in the butter with your fingertips until it looks like breadcrumbs.",
   "Squeeze the grated carrot in your hands to get rid of extra juice, then stir it in with the thyme and most of the cheese.",
   "Beat the egg with the milk and keep a spoonful back. Pour in the rest and mix with a knife to a soft, slightly sticky dough.",
   "Tip onto a floured surface, pat into a round about 3cm thick and cut into 8 wedges. Set on the tray, brush with the saved egg and scatter over the last of the cheese.",
   "Bake for 15 to 18 minutes, until risen and golden. Cool for 10 minutes, then eat warm with butter."
  ]
